       "title": "Square root functions",
       "page": 62,
       "body": [
        "The basic square root function is f(x) = √x. Its graph starts at (0, 0) and rises more and more slowly to the right. The general form f(x) = a√(x − h) + k moves the starting point ",
        "**Domain:** the expression under the root must be ≥ 0, so for √(x − h) the domain is x ≥ h. **Range** (with a > 0): y ≥ k."
       ]
